{
 "version": 1,
 "summary": "The longest run of 1s after flipping at most `k` zeros is the longest window containing at most `k` zeros. Grow\nthe window right, counting zeros; when the count exceeds `k`, advance the left edge until a zero leaves. O(n).",
 "question": [
  {
   "md": "Turn at most `k` zeros of `status` into ones. Return the longest run of consecutive ones you can get.\n\n- **n up to 10⁵.**"
  }
 ],
 "think": [
  {
   "md": "`status = [1, 1, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1]`, `k = 2` → **8**.\n\nWhich zeros to patch? Only those inside the run we end up with. So a run is achievable exactly when it holds\nat most `k` zeros: we're looking for the longest window with at most `k` zeros. A sub-window of a valid window\nis valid, so the left edge only ever moves right."
  },
